  "problem": "Payer Transparency in Coverage indexes could substitute employer plan IDs, insurer identities and hospital identities. Shared files could be fetched repeatedly and lose plan associations. Inaccessible bulk files could drop out of the frozen 10-entity denominator. Hospital HPT schemas could be treated as payer TiC. Allowed-amount files could be treated as validated by the in-network parser.",
  "resulting_behavior": "Payer index parsing lives in packages/connectors/mrf/payer-index.mjs because identity is WP7-sealed. Frozen 10 HIOS issuer IDs are consumed without replacement or silent deduplication. Employer plan ID, insurer identity and hospital identity cannot be substituted. The same file linked by many plans is fetched once but retains all supported plan associations. All ten reporting entities are accounted for; an inaccessible bulk file remains a valid documented route with failed sample state. Hospital HPT and payer TiC schemas remain separate. Allowed-amount files are discoverable without pretending the in-network parser validates them. Last-good generation live-2026-09-03-85b50522b420 is unchanged.",
